  "body": "Run the whole app from a single `npm run dev` — signed in as the real admin, reading/writing **live Cosmos**. Same setup chess-tactics uses: \"vite alone is full prod from dev.\"\n\n## What it does\n\n- A dev-only vite plugin (`apply:'serve'`) spawns `backend/server.js` as a child on an **OS-assigned free port** (parallel worktrees never collide), tied to vite's lifecycle — relaunches on crash, dies when vite exits.\n- The child points at **live Cosmos** (`COSMOS_DB_ENDPOINT`, passwordless via your `az login`) with `DEV_AUTH` set to the **real identity** (admin); vite proxies `/api` to it.\n- `DEV_NO_BACKEND=1` opts out to the frontend-only sql.js snapshot (anonymous).\n\n## Prod-safe\n\nThe plugin is absent from `vite build` (gated on `command === 'serve'` + `apply:'serve'`), and the prod backend never sets `DEV_AUTH` or `COSMOS_DB_ENDPOINT` — so this is entirely inert in production.\n\n## Verified\n\n- `/api/auth/me` → real admin identity (not a placeholder)\n- `/api/current-day` → live Cosmos data\n- `npm run build` succeeds\n",
